# English table: same control codes as jp.tbl; letters, digits and punctuation reuse the Latin/symbol codes,
# redrawn narrow by fonts/vwf.txt (tools/font.py). Kana and kanji codes keep their Japanese glyphs.
00={br}
# 01 stays the JP's 12 px blank (indents, column padding, the engine's own field padding); the English space is a
# 4 px glyph drawn over the unused hiragana code 02.
01={blank}
02=\s
A3=0
A4=1
A5=2
A6=3
A7=4
A8=5
A9=6
AA=7
AB=8
AC=9
AD=-
